  ## Tracks

  **Track 1 — v6.0.4 emergency patch team analysis**
  - Team: Architect + Builder + Helix + Jinx + Loid
  - Goal: produce implementation plan for v6.0.4 (drop framework aspect-coverage block when no claimant; paradigm doctor surfaces metrics; paradigm shift nominates Rune; CLAUDE.md reframe)
  - Constraints from TD-2026-04-26-284: Advise-default, archetype-default claims (write the schema even though full claims work ships v6.1), soft-block held for v6.1, tier split deferred to track 2

  **Track 2 — Tier-1/Tier-2 notebook split design pass**
  - Lead: Loid (notebook architecture owner)
  - Goal: schema for `tier: transferable | project-local`, migration plan, promotion criteria, interaction with archetype-default authority
  - Must complete before v6.1 phase 13

  **Track 3 — Paradigm University agents course (Phase A only)**
  - Team: Sheila (educator, lead) + Scholar (paired via partners primitive) + Loid
  - Phase A scope (safe, won't mutate at v6.1): archetype model, identity (id/nickname/archetype), 21-agent roster + roles, partners primitive (Scholar+Sheila as canonical), how to roster/bench/activate, paradigm shift auto-rostering, orchestration modes (faceted vs sequential)
  - Phase B (Rune authority modes, soft-block usage, tier semantics, cross-project compounding) HELD until v6.1 lock
  - Forcing function noted: shipping U content before v6.1 stability = stale curriculum risk (per Lore-is-critical-infrastructure feedback)

  ## Tracking convention this session
  - Each track records its findings as a lore entry (insight type) with `tags: [v6.0.4-track, v6.1-tier-split, agents-course-phase-a]` respectively
  - Decisions go through paradigm_decision_record (auto-companion lore)
  - Final synthesis lore at session close linking all three tracks
